silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_diagram_n a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "ConcreteAnchorDiagramNExample" .
silm:instances_papers_15_chapters_01_sections_01_concrete_anchor_diagram_n silm:hasExample "In 'ConcreteAnchorDiagramN', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, At n=1, the source functor whose admitted legs are: the Cat anchor, the species-type leg, the head observation HeadObs77, the body-mass quality BodyMassQuality77. At n=2, additionally the microchip identifier MicrochipIdentifier9. The diagram is finite at every stage but unbounded across the limit.." .
